※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4218 LANG_TYPE_APPROXIMATE_NEEDS_A_FLOAT

※ Two integers are equal or they are not: there is no error in one for a
※ tolerance to allow for, so the approximate comparisons have nothing to ask
※ of them.  A truth value is not ordered at all.

let a: u8 = 3u8
let b: u8 = 3u8
let ready: bool = true

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    @[ignore(5005)]
    a ≅ b
    @[ignore(5005)]
    ready ≇ ready
    0u8
